  "summary": "I added a \"Close portal\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`. Typecheck passes and the render shows the scene intact with the button under the canvas. I haven't clicked the button, since the tools can't click, so closing and reopening is untested.\n\nOn close, the vortex disc, all four particle groups and the three portal lights are hidden with `setVisible(false)`. `window.__TASK_STATE__` becomes `{ portalActive: false, particleCount: 0, time }` and the label changes to \"Open portal\". I also keep refreshing the state every frame while the portal is closed. The camera sway and the ring runes keep animating while it's closed.\n\nOn reopen, everything is shown again and the particles restart with fresh random lifetimes. State goes back to `portalActive: true` and `particleCount` 196 (150 spiral particles plus 46 motes), and the label reads \"Close portal\"."
}